<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 12 February, from 1502 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1502 <span class="tih-ago">524 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Castile orders its Muslims to convert or leave</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A decree of Isabella I gave the Muslims of Castile a choice between baptism and exile. Most converted, becoming Moriscos, whose descendants were expelled from Spain in 1609-14.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Moriscos</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1554 <span class="tih-ago">472 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lady Jane Grey is executed at the Tower</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The teenage Protestant queen, deposed after nine days in 1553, was beheaded on Mary I's orders following Wyatt's Rebellion. Her husband Guildford Dudley was executed the same morning.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1809 <span class="tih-ago">217 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abraham Lincoln is born in Kentucky</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Born in a one-room log cabin near Hodgenville, Lincoln was largely self-taught. As the 16th President he led the Union through the Civil War and helped bring about the end of slavery.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1809 <span class="tih-ago">217 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles Darwin is born in Shrewsbury</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Born on the same day as Lincoln, Darwin sailed on HMS Beagle and developed the theory of evolution by natural selection, published in 'On the Origin of Species' in 1859.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1818 <span class="tih-ago">208 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chile proclaims its independence from Spain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bernardo O'Higgins formally proclaimed Chile's independence on the first anniversary of the victory at Chacabuco. Spanish forces were decisively beaten at Maipú that April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1912 <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Puyi, the last Emperor of China, abdicates</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Empress Dowager Longyu issued the edict of abdication for the six-year-old Puyi. The fall of the Qing ended more than two thousand years of imperial rule in China.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/moscow" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1974 <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet authorities arrest Aleksandr Solzhenitsyn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Weeks after 'The Gulag Archipelago' appeared in Paris, the Nobel laureate was arrested in Moscow and charged with treason. The next day he was stripped of citizenship and deported to West Germany.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
